Z||000005||Kelvin Vivian||12-15-2001||11:02 PM||||When looking for the car you want, the best thing to have is patience.  Good deals spring up every now-and-then... Check out <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com," TARGET=_blank>www.classifieds2000.com,</A>  <A HREF="http://www.autotrader.com," TARGET=_blank>www.autotrader.com,</A>  and my favorite - go to <A HREF="http://www.google.com" TARGET=_blank>www.google.com</A>  and search on "T Top Fiero for sale", and see what comes up.  Also check your local newspaper classified ads, that's how I found my 88 T-Top.  <P>KV<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd<BR>88 GT T-Top, 5-spd<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.printroom.com/_vti_bin/ViewImage.dll?userid=no_18&album_id=36084&image_id=3&courtesy=1">     <BR>88 GT, 5-spd<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||14
Z||000006||jelly2m8||12-16-2001||12:32 AM||||Just keep looking and keep your eyes open.<P> Back in late october I lucked out on a 88 T-Top coupe for 300 bux on e-bay!<P> The body and interior is rough, but mechanically it is near mint, the best I have seen so far.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
